	)
	(text "ADC Design Notes\n\n1. Sampling rate allocation\nThe RP2350 internal ADC runs at 500 kS/s (48 MHz ADC clock, 96 cycles\nper conversion, 2 µs per sample). Six channels are sampled in round-robin\nmode, so each channel gets about 83.3 kS/s (one full round takes 12 µs),\nand the per-channel Nyquist frequency is about 41.7 kHz.\n\n2. Low-pass filter cutoff\nEach photodiode channel uses a 200 Ω sense resistor followed by an RC\nlow-pass filter (1 kΩ + 1 µF). The time constant is about 1.2 ms\n(including the 200 Ω sense resistor), giving a cutoff frequency of about\n133 Hz (159 Hz if only the 1 kΩ is counted). Attenuation at the Nyquist\nfrequency is about 50 dB.\n\n3. Estimated maximum current and voltage\nAt perihelion (solar irradiance about 1408 W/m²), the estimated BPW34\nphotocurrent is 4 to 9 mA (extrapolated from the datasheet, not a\ndatasheet value). The design limit is 12 mA, which gives a maximum\nsense voltage of about 2.4 V with the 200 Ω resistor, below the 3.3 V\nsupply and ADC input limit.\n\n4. ADC choice\nThe design currently uses the RP2350 internal ADC to keep the design\nsimple, with no external ADC. If the internal ADC turns out to be\nunusable, one of the following external ADCs can be added:\n- MCP3208 (SPI, breadboard-friendly package, external voltage reference)\n  https://ww1.microchip.com/downloads/aemDocuments/documents/APID/\nProductDocuments/DataSheets/21298e.pdf\n- ADS7828 (I²C, surface-mount, internal voltage reference)\n  https://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/ads7828.pdf"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 212.598 372.872 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "aa2450ff-fcfa-4bd1-a175-044d1894b5fb")
	)
	(text "NC"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 333.756 188.468 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "acd047b5-5891-4561-9738-c78ebfa271d2")
	)
