	(text "LAYOUT GUIDELINES\nSeparate RF and digital circuits into different PCB regions.\nIt is necessary to maintain 50-ohm impedance throughout the entire RF signal path. Try keeping the RF signal path as\nshort as possible.\nDo not route the RF signal line near noisy sources such as digital signals, oscillators, switching power supplies, or other\nRF transmitting circuit. Do not route the RF signal under or over any other components (including Orion B16), or other\nsignal traces. Do not route the RF signal path on an inner layer of a multi-layer PCB to minimize signal loss.\nAvoid sharp bends for RF signal path. Make two 45-deg bends or a circular bend instead of a single 90-degree bend if\nneeded.\nAvoid vias with RF signal path whenever possible. Every via adds inductive impedance. Vias are acceptable for\nconnecting the RF grounds between different layers. Each of the module's ground pins should have short trace tying\nimmediately to the ground plane below through a via.\nThe bypass capacitors should be low ESR ceramic types and located directly adjacent to the pin they are for."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 312.42 244.856 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "d9f3f5d2-2c77-4922-b443-90a2d7d147c4")
	)
	(text "JST Debug Connector"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 120.65 335.28 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "dc72f01a-0614-47e9-beba-1fb91d931e78")
	)
	(text "- Twist the two wires from each BPW34 together to minimize loop area; \navoid routing them separately.\n- Keep sensor wiring away from magnetorquer coils, driver circuits, \nDC/DC inductors, and switching nodes.\n- Place the analog front end close to the sensor connector to minimize\n trace length between the connector and sensitive input nodes.\n- Maintain a continuous ground reference and use component placement \nand routing to control high-current return paths. "
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 209.55 116.84 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
